ci(129,fate='Sullivan (1977), Theorem 8.1 p. 301 and Theorem 10.1 p. 307, proves rational minimal-model comparison for nilpotent finite-type objects and spaces. The nonnilpotent real statement labelled “Theorem” 8.1′, pp. 303–304, explicitly leaves its continuous-cohomology part (v) incompletely proved. This matches the distinction on the English donor leaf; it neither settles arbitrary fundamental groups nor identifies the author of N27.',search_record='MID-S16,MID-S19,MID-S20')
ci(141,status_on_pages='theorem stated; proof and implications belong to the donor work',fate='SGA7 IX Theorem 11.5, printed p. 455, identifies the ℓ-primary component group with the cokernel of the monodromy lattice map and yields perfect component duality for semistable reduction over a henselian trait. Remark 11.5.2(a) explicitly deduces rational nondegeneracy, including ℓ=p, without using the deeper Theorem 10.4. Remark (b) then uses 10.4 for a single integral, ℓ-independent pairing. General non-semistable component-pairing questions are separate.')
pr(42,as_he_states='The component-cokernel theorem should give the claimed duality, including the p-primary part; the rational monodromy pairing must be separating.',plausible_today='Use SGA7 IX Theorem 11.5 over a henselian trait with semistable reduction. Its Remark 11.5.2(a) gives rational nondegeneracy, including ℓ=p, without Theorem 10.4; the integral and ℓ-independent refinement in (b) additionally uses 10.4.',state_of_art='Published SGA7 IX 11.5 and 11.5.2(a)–(b), printed p. 455, distinguish these two results explicitly.',why_open='This is a deferred argument inside the donor work; the published source resolves it and explicitly warns against treating rational nondegeneracy as dependent on the deeper integral theorem.')
